## WAVE-38-QUEUE-NAMES-UNTRACKED - REGISTERED
{
 "id": "WAVE-38-QUEUE-NAMES-UNTRACKED",
 "title": "Two of the queued LOOPS/AGGREGATE cards' target names reach no tracker, and one is classified as a rule not work",
 "why": "MEASURED by card STABILITY-REEVAL-3 (wave 38), step 4. The queued compiler cards name their targets by residual: LOOPS-ON-COMPOSED-ROUTES by STRING-CONCAT-LOOP-WINDOW, SLICE-PERMISSIONS-LOOP-WINDOW and WRITE-LEND-RELEND; AGGREGATE-OWNED-FIELD by its own name. In named_followups: WRITE-LEND-RELEND is PRESENT; STRING-CONCAT-LOOP-WINDOW and AGGREGATE-OWNED-FIELD are ABSENT (only mentioned inside other entries' why texts, which scripts/reconciliation_sweep.py says is not tracking); SLICE-PERMISSIONS-LOOP-WINDOW is one of the nine names CONSTRAINT-NAMED-BOUNDARIES-NOT-OPEN-WORK classifies as a RULE the constraint imposes, which 'a card that lifts must name then'. So a card sized from the tracker finds one of its three targets, and a card sized from the constraint finds a rule. This is WAVE-36-CARDS-UNCHARTERED's shape one wave later. Step-4 measurement for the briefs: on both routes the window is computed over TOP-LEVEL event indices only (std_buffer.rs lend_windows :965-1054, last_use over Store/Load/Extent/Release/Lend with through = unwrap_or(index); std_string.rs last_view_uses :1057 and :1509), so a loan used only inside a Repeat body would close before the loop opens and every owner write in the body would be admitted - which is why both Repeat refusals (std_buffer.rs:1926-1944, std_string.rs:1814-1843) sit BEFORE the window computation and must not be reordered; and constraint 15k's 'a record contributes no ownership operation' is an explicit no-op arm (std_buffer.rs:914-918) over an owner vocabulary that is a plain String everywhere (ownership.rs:169-176, :242, :845), so AGGREGATE-OWNED-FIELD is an IR card before it is a route card and Q055's buffer-at-a-field-position refusal is the gate it must knowingly lift. DISCHARGE: register STRING-CONCAT-LOOP-WINDOW and AGGREGATE-OWNED-FIELD with the discharge conditions above, or extend CONSTRAINT-NAMED-BOUNDARIES-NOT-OPEN-WORK to name them and say why the queued cards are not their work.",
 "source": "docs/reports/stability-reeval-3/README.md",
 "recorded_by": "STABILITY-REEVAL-3"
}
