 "title": "The 14-row Clang early-return shape is a 750-guard family, and no gate.json records Clang presence",
 "why": "MEASURED by card STABILITY-REEVAL-3 (wave 38): rg -c 'if !clang_available()' over crates/ and compiler/ totals 750 early-return guards across 79 test files (publication_custody.rs 36, neutral_expression_positions.rs 32, may_alias_boundary.rs 32, ... scalar_route_exit_edge.rs 11). RETURN-CALL-TESTS-CLANG-GUARDED-GREEN (firing #2) named the shape on one file of 14 rows; it is the crate convention. On a Clang-less host every one reports ok having measured nothing, and no close's gate.json records whether Clang was present when its workspace count was taken - the ten keys are counts and exits, so a 4,637-green figure taken without Clang would be indistinguishable from one taken with it. This card recorded clang-version.txt (Ubuntu clang 21.1.8, QCORE_CLANG unset) beside its own gate as the cheapest form of the discharge. DISCHARGE: a clang presence key (present/absent plus version) in the close's gate.json, checked by the generator the way lean_audits now is; OR one shared helper that reports Clang absence as ignored so the count moves visibly; and the 14-row entry re-scoped to the family or retired into this one.",
